  "summary_en": "Vietnam's Law on Artificial Intelligence (No. 134/2025/QH15), adopted 10 December 2025 and effective 1 March 2026. It sets human-centred principles, risk-proportionate management, prohibited conduct, incident reporting, conformity assessment, a national AI database and infrastructure, sandboxes and incentives. Defence and security uses are excluded.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Human-centred principles requiring human control and ability to intervene in AI systems",
   "Risk-proportionate management, with stricter controls in health and education",
   "Prohibits deceptive deepfakes, exploiting vulnerable groups and obstructing human oversight",
   "One-stop AI portal and national AI database for classification notices, incident reports and conformity results",
   "Effective 1 March 2026 with 12-18 month transition for existing systems; defence/security excluded"
